//
// Phase B runtime seam: host-only rules tests.
//
// Covers the BO liveness allocator (live ranges, slot sharing, the content-keyed
// static pool, the dirty-bit discipline) and runlist aggregation (submission
// grouping, the ELF-vs-xclbin argument ABI, the dispatch vector). The rules they
// check are written down in
// docs/plans/transformer-layer-execution-studies/05b-phase-b-buffer-rules.md.
//
// No NPU and no XRT: BoPool takes its allocator as a callable and the ABI
// binding is tested against a fake run object, so this sits alongside the
// compile-only kernel gate and requires neither `ryzen_ai_npu2` nor `peano`.
// The hardware half of Phase B is `make runlist-gate`, which is not a lit test
// because it needs a device and takes minutes.
//
// The test files carry no framework dependency -- pytest is not installed in the
// sandbox venv -- so they run as plain scripts and print a pass count.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_bo_pool.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=POOL
// POOL: 33/33 passed
//
// `[2026-08-25]` 35 -> 40, item 14's review round (blocking): the ELF is the
// ABI ground truth. `dispatch.elf_arg_count` reads the kernel's buffer-arg
// count from the binary's own .dynsym (numeric names ARE the arg indices) and
// `validate_arg_count` refuses -- BEFORE any device work, at load_and_run, the
// one chokepoint every load path dispatches through -- a call that does not
// match it, in either direction, plus a manifest n_args contradicting its ELF.
// The five pin the parser on synthetic ELFs, both refusal directions (the devq
// 583 unbound-scratch class and its inverse), the stale-manifest clause with
// the manifest-only fallback, and by source that the check precedes
// ensure_loaded and that compile time records n_args.
// `[2026-08-26]` 40 -> 42, queue item 19 (doc 56 H3 stages 1-2): the `xrt.run`
// cache. Building a run and binding its arguments costs 57.5 us per call
// (devq 622) against 16.8 us for the submission a runlist removes, so a
// 57-submission decode token pays ~3.3 ms for bindings that never change; the
// cache is worth -2.2 ms/token measured (devq 623) and +4.1 % tok/s end to end
// (devq 624). The two tests pin where reuse is legal and where it is REFUSED:
// ON in `load_and_run`, one run per (kernel, bo_key) while that bo_key's BO
// list stands, discarded by `xrt.kernel` identity when a context is evicted
// and reloaded; OFF by default in `run_sequence`, because a sequence's runs
// can only be keyed on the pool object and the entry would then keep an
// evicted pool's BOs alive -- defeating exactly the per-dispatch pool eviction
// `pattern/offload` is defined by. Driven against a fake pyxrt, no device.
//
// `[2026-08-26]` 42 -> 53, queue item 28: the herd-rows lock-race coupling. A
// herd occupying more than ONE CORE ROW hangs the device in `matvec.py`'s GEMV
// form (ERT_CMD_STATE_TIMEOUT, item 27 section 6.1, bisected devq 673/674 --
// only `use_lock_race_condition_fix` unblocks it). The row count belongs to the
// builder and the lock fix to the caller, so the rule is enforced where both
// are in scope, `KernelCache.compile_and_cache`, and it REFUSES before a
// backend is constructed rather than letting the device time out after a
// multi-minute compile.
//
// `[2026-08-27]` THE RULE FAILS CLOSED, and the tests that say so are the
// point of the count going 52 -> 53. Item 28's first guard filtered on
// `link_with == "mv.o"` and converted every unreadable geometry into "one
// row" -- so the same builder reached through a renamed micro-kernel object
// (this tree renames them routinely: `mv_heads_hd128.o`,
// `mv_int4_bf16_gemv_gs128_k1024.o`) sailed past and would have hung, which is
// the worst possible direction for a hazard guard. There is no honest
// structural discriminator either: MEASURED on the shipped modules, the
// prefill GEMM herds share one L2 A panel per column across all four rows --
// the very shape item 27 blamed -- and they do not hang. So the default is to
// refuse, geometry that cannot be decoded counts as multi-row, and the
// exemption is a registry of kernels MEASURED green (membership itself
// measured, by building every shipped model's modules). Pinned here: the
// geometry read including the async-token operand form; every unreadable form
// raising instead of reading as one row; a multi-row herd refused whatever
// object it links; undecidable geometry refused; both fix versions accepted;
// exemption only by exact name plus the one generated `flash_attn_ctx*`
// family; the landed `lm_head_gemv` NOT exempt but carrying the fix; and the
// refusal happening ahead of any compile.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_dispatch.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DISPATCH
// DISPATCH: 53/53 passed
//
// `[2026-08-21]` Doc 56 H0: the analytical planner's host gates -- the two golden
// graphs pinned, each model's plan reproducing its shipped ELF sequence / launch
// counts / NPU-CPU split, profiles.skip_reason reproduced over every family, the
// caps cross-checked against the study constants, the tile solver ranked against
// the registry with every mismatch in a named class.
// `[2026-08-25]` 10 -> 11, queue item 16 (doc 56 H1b): plan_ubatch_prefill --
// the chunked-prefill plan composes per-chunk stages (the FA artifact named
// per context, rectangular past chunk 1), derives the totals the model
// runner's live checks enforce (169 submissions / 171 host ops at 2 x 512),
// hashes as its own identity, degenerates to the whole plan at one chunk,
// and refuses a partial chunk (no padding path).
// `[2026-08-26]` 11 -> 12, queue item 17 (doc 56 H2a): the w4_decode decode
// plan names the SHIPPED int4 sequence (rms_qkv_int4_rope 6 / o_gemv_ffn_int4
// 3 / lm_head_gemv 8 -- 33 submissions, 152 launches, 34 host ops per token)
// with the quant contract named per int4 GEMV, hashes apart from bf16, keeps
// prefill bf16 (dequantized weights), and refuses a qk-norm model until H2b.
// `[2026-08-26]` 13 -> 14, queue item 19 review (finding 6): the O2 pair
// aggregation is a RECORDED rejected candidate on every decode plan, carrying
// its measurement (-1.427/-1.484 ms/token, devq 623/624, ~864 MB of doubled
// weights) -- and recording it does NOT move the plan hash, because `rejected`
// is outside `plan()`'s hashed body. That second clause is the property worth
// pinning: a measured negative can never invalidate an artifact set keyed by a
// plan sha.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/plan/test_plan.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAN
// PLAN: 14/14 passed
//
// `[2026-08-23]` Doc 57 O1 second half: the Qwen3 QKV stage's two host ABIs --
// the driver's argument helper follows QWEN3_RMS_QKV_LAUNCHES, the 2-launch
// shapes, the augmented weight's (tag, kind) per row, the slot gather as the
// inverse of the device's slot layout.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_decode_qkv4.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=QKV4
// QKV4: 4/4 passed
